      "comment": "A country takes a preposition: <span lang=\"la\">in Sinās</span>, <span lang=\"la\">in Sinīs</span>, <span lang=\"la\">ex Sinīs</span>. Properly the people, the Chinese, used as the name of the land: <span lang=\"la\">Sinārum imperātōrēs</span> (Wolff, in M-O). Modern Latin often writes a long <span lang=\"la\">ī</span>; we leave it unmarked, having found no quantity in our sources."
